          "story": "3-WOOD B6 — PROMISING CARRY, PARTIAL SAMPLE. Six retained visible shots average 185.1 yd carry / 218.9 total. Best five average 191.2 carry; longest is 195.3. Shot 7 is a clear carry mishit; shots 5–6 have no distance. Five further shots were off-screen. Mean launch is 10.6° and face-to-path +2.9°; delivery and strike vary. Repeat B6 with the same balls and settings, capturing all rows, before attributing changes to the sleeve or wrist feel.\n\nHI-TOE 58° — ESTABLISH THE NORMAL FLIGHT. Five retained shots average 75.2 carry / 82.4 total, with 34.4° launch. Shots 5 and 7 show 11.8° and 4.1° launch and impact 22/27 mm below center; these reviewed thin/skull outliers are held out of normal-flight averages. The 130.2-yard finish is not a wedge stock yardage. For the next block, repeat a comfortable swing and track carry spread before testing separate partial-swing distances.",
